# AI Autopilot Build Sequence

This is the build order for making MedSpa Growth Engine run on autopilot after the owner completes the required setup.

## Phase 1: Control Center

Goal:

- One place for leads, outreach, replies, calls, clients, and owner briefs.

Build:

- Import `AI_LEAD_PIPELINE_TEMPLATE.csv`.
- Import `AI_OPERATOR_TASK_BOARD.csv`.
- Create Outreach Log table.
- Create Replies table.
- Create Call Briefs table.
- Create Clients table.

Acceptance:

- Every lead has status and next action.
- Every contacted lead has next follow-up date.
- Every reply has classification.
- Every booked call has a brief.

## Phase 2: Research Engine

Goal:

- No generic outreach leaves the system.

Build:

- Lead sourcing workflow.
- Enrichment workflow.
- Fit score.
- Pain hypothesis.
- Personalization line.
- Research Needed queue.

Acceptance:

- 10 sample leads researched.
- No invented facts.
- Every first-touch message uses one real observation.

## Phase 3: Outreach Queue

Goal:

- Messages and follow-ups happen on time.

Build:

- First-touch generator.
- Follow-up generator.
- Approval queue.
- Send limits.
- Bounce handling.
- Unsubscribe handling.

Acceptance:

- First campaign approved.
- Test sends log correctly.
- Follow-up dates populate correctly.
- Opt-out stops all future touches.

## Phase 4: Reply Triage

Goal:

- Hot replies are surfaced fast.

Build:

- Gmail/DM/manual reply intake.
- Reply classification.
- Suggested response.
- Owner-needed flag.
- Daily owner brief.

Acceptance:

- Hot, warm, objection, not now, unsubscribe, bad fit, and complaint replies route correctly.

## Phase 5: Sales Assist

Goal:

- Owner enters every call prepared.

Build:

- Call brief generator.
- Demo route generator.
- Post-call recap draft.
- Proposal follow-up tracker.

Acceptance:

- Every booked call gets a brief.
- Every completed call gets next step and follow-up date.

## Phase 6: Delivery Assist

Goal:

- Closed client becomes a clean install.

Build:

- Sales handoff.
- Client delivery board.
- Missing-access tracker.
- QA checklist.
- Client kickoff draft.

Acceptance:

- Paid client creates tasks automatically.
- Missing access is chased.
- Go-live cannot happen without QA checklist.

## Phase 7: Client Success Autopilot

Goal:

- Clients see value and risks are caught early.

Build:

- Weekly report draft.
- Workflow error monitor.
- Client health score.
- Churn-risk alerts.
- Monthly improvement idea.

Acceptance:

- Every live client gets weekly report draft.
- Error alerts create tasks.
- Churn-risk clients are escalated to owner.

## Phase 8: Ads Autopilot

Goal:

- Paid ads use proven hooks, not guesses.

Build:

- Winning hook extractor.
- Ad concept generator.
- Creative script generator.
- Ad review dashboard.
- Spend approval gate.

Acceptance:

- Ads do not run until outbound proves hooks.
- Owner approves spend, claims, and creative.

## Launch Readiness Gate

The autopilot is live-ready when:

- Lead tracker exists.
- Research gate works.
- Outreach approval queue works.
- Send limits are configured.
- Unsubscribe handling is tested.
- Reply triage works.
- Daily owner brief works.
- Call brief generator works.
- Delivery board works.
- Client weekly report workflow works.
- Secrets are not stored in public files or browser-only storage.

## Owner Setup Dependencies

The owner must provide:

- Email inbox.
- Calendar link.
- Approved offer/pricing.
- Payment/contract path.
- Target markets.
- Sending limits.
- Compliance preference.
- Automation platform credentials.

Once these are done, the AI operator can run the machine daily and only call the owner in when needed.
